  "raw_text": "No. The timing shows correlation, not causation.\n\nThe update is a plausible suspect, but establishing causation requires more evidence—for example:\n\n- Relevant errors or logs linking the failure to the update\n- Reproduction of the failure after applying the update\n- Resolution after rolling the update back\n- Similar failures on other updated machines\n- Ruling out hardware faults, configuration changes, workload changes, or other intervening causes\n\nThe proper conclusion is: **the update may have caused the failure and should be investigated, but timing alone does not prove it.**",
